From: Ryan Zegalia <ryanzegalia@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: GPU passive trip at the factory 95 C

The eight gpuss zones brake the GPU (devfreq cooling) at a passive trip of
85 C. On the actively cooled AYN Thor that brake held the GPU below its
680 MHz top for 70 % of a sustained load with the fan at full speed
(2026-10-20, 615/680 MHz flapping). The Thor's own Android device tree
(AYN vendor_boot, Kalama QCM and KalamaP QCS tables) throttles the GPU at
a 95 C junction limit (tj_cfg, all eight gpuss zones, bound to kgsl).

Use the factory 95 C. The hot (90 C) and critical (110 C, shutdown) trips
are unchanged, as are the CPU zones (hardware LMh limits the CPU).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi	2026-10-20 09:25:09.629798791 -0400
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi	2026-10-20 09:25:09.630333433 -0400
@@ -6938,7 +6938,7 @@
 
 			trips {
 				gpu0_alert0: trip-point0 {
-					temperature = <85000>;
+					temperature = <95000>;
 					hysteresis = <1000>;
 					type = "passive";
 				};
@@ -6971,7 +6971,7 @@
 
 			trips {
 				gpu1_alert0: trip-point0 {
-					temperature = <85000>;
+					temperature = <95000>;
